abstract: >-
  Localized linear excitations of a classical complex scalar Q-ball in three
  spatial dimensions with potential U(S) = S - S^2 + S^3/2. Computer-assisted
  existence arguments (interval arithmetic plus analytic exterior estimates) for
  two radial modes and one dipole mode on the infinite radial domain; a numerical
  radial sequence with candidates up to index eighteen; a thin-wall
  phase-matching interpretation with an unfitted planar spacing candidate; and a
  conditional second-harmonic obstruction to a specified localized nonlinear
  continuation. Version 0.53 states the radial ladder as an explicit conjecture,
  adds a part on limitations and open problems, a numerical evaluation of the
  charge slope dQ/domega at the three certified backgrounds, and a matching
  calculation that raises ladder indices 5 and 11-14 to resolved numerical
  windings; companion archive revision 3. No certificate, lemma or certified
  enclosure is changed. Preprint, not peer reviewed. Produced with extensive use
  of AI tools (Claude, Anthropic; Codex, OpenAI) under the author's direction;
  an external assessment made with Gemini (Google) was taken into account.
keywords:
  - Q-ball
  - bound state in the continuum
  - interval arithmetic
  - computer-assisted proof
